			"crowdNoiseIntensity": 0, // [Blind Test] Volume density level of collective human crowd noise from 0 to 5. Count only non-primary human group sounds such as public chatter, cheering, applause, laughter, screaming, yelling, or crowd murmurs. Do NOT count the main speaker(s), narration, dialogue, or BGM vocals. 0 = no crowd noise, 1 = distant faint murmur, 2 = low but noticeable crowd bed, 3 = moderate crowd noise clearly present under the main signal, 4 = loud crowd noise frequently competing with speech/music, 5 = deafening crowd noise that dominates or masks the primary signal. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
			"ambientNoiseDetails": ["None"], //  [Blind Test] Background environmental noise floor category. Select only audible environmental floor, not intended BGM and not intentional SFX. Use ["StudioSilence"] when the track is post-produced or very clean with no meaningful environmental floor. Use ["Indoor/RoomTone"] only when room resonance, air-conditioning, indoor hum, or enclosed-space tone is audibly present. Use ["None"] when no ambient layer can be detected. Predefined choices: [Urban/Traffic, Industrial/Manufacturing, Construction, Nature/Outdoor, Indoor/RoomTone, StudioSilence, Domestic/Neighborhood, Chatter, Commercial/Recreational, Other, Unknown, None]. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options.
			"ambientNoiseIntensity": 0, //  [Blind Test] Intensity of the continuous or semi-continuous environmental noise floor from 0 to 5. Score only stable background ambience such as traffic hum, wind bed, room tone, air-conditioning, machinery hum, restaurant ambience, vehicle cabin noise, rain, or outdoor environmental floor. Do NOT count sudden incidental noises, crowd reactions, BGM, speech, or intentional post-production SFX. 0 = no audible ambient noise / studio-clean silence, 1 = very faint ambient floor with no interference, 2 = low ambient noise clearly below the main signal, 3 = moderate ambient noise noticeable but not masking the main signal, 4 = loud ambient noise frequently competing with speech/music, 5 = dominant ambient noise that strongly masks the primary signal. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
			"incidentalNoiseDetails": ["None"], //  [Blind Test] Incidental non-designed noise events captured in the recording. These are real-world, non-post-produced, non-musical, non-crowd, short-duration or irregular sound events. These are different from continuous ambient noise and different from intentional post-production sound effects. Predefined choices: ["Object Impact / Thud / Drop", "Door / Cabinet Open-Close", "Footsteps", "Wood Products Bump / Movemen", "Ceramics / Glass  Clink", "Paper / Page Rustle", "Plastic / Bag Rustle", "Clothing / Fabric Rustle",  "Zipper Sound", "Metal  Bump ", "Handheld / Microphone Handling Noise", "Camera Shutter / Camera Operation", "Phone Vibration", "Notification Sound", "Mechanical Click / Latch", "Liquid Pour / Splash", "Food Bite / Crunch", "Vehicle Horn / Engine", "Animal Sound / Barking", "Sudden Wind Burst", "Firecrackers / Fireworks / Explosion", "Electrical Buzz / Glitch Artifact", "Recording Pop / Plosive", "Other", "Unknown", "None"]. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
			"incidentalNoiseIntensity": 0, // "[Blind Test] Intensity and masking impact of incidental non-designed noise events from 0 to 5. Score only real-world captured noise events, not BGM, not crowd noise, not continuous ambient beds, and not intentional post-production SFX. 0 = no incidental noise events, 1 = very faint or rare incidental sounds with no interference, 2 = low-level incidental sounds occasionally audible but clearly below the main signal, 3 = moderate incidental sounds noticeable and sometimes competing with the main signal, 4 = loud incidental sounds frequently interrupting or masking speech/music, 5 = extreme incidental noise events that dominate the mix or severely obscure the primary signal. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
			"SignalToNoiseRatio": 0, // [Blind Test] Perceived signal-to-noise ratio of the overall audio track from 0 to 5. This is an approximate perceptual rating, not a precise engineering measurement. Score how clearly the intended primary signal—speech, narration, music, or other designed program audio—stands above ONLY these unwanted noise sources: crowdNoiseDetail, ambientNoiseDetails, and incidentalNoiseDetails. Do NOT count intended BGM, intentional post-production soundEffectsDetails, clean room tone, normal speech-music overlap, or designed transition sounds as noise. 0 = completely no sound, 1 = extremely poor SNR / primary signal heavily masked by crowd, ambient, or incidental noise, 2 = low SNR / unwanted noise often competes with the primary signal, 3 = moderate SNR / some unwanted noise is present but the primary signal remains understandable, 4 = high SNR / clean signal with only minor or faint unwanted noise, 5 = excellent SNR / pristine or studio-clean signal with no meaningful unwanted crowd, ambient, or incidental noise. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
			"soundEffectsDetails": ["None"], // [Blind Test] Intentional post-production sound effects added for editing, emphasis, transition, humor, interface simulation, or dramatic impact. These are deliberately designed or inserted audio effects, NOT real-world incidental noises captured by the microphone. Do NOT include door sounds, object bumps, footsteps, utensil clinks, camera shutter sounds, bag rustles, or environmental noises here unless they are clearly stylized post-production effects. Predefined choices: ["Whoosh / Transition SFX", "Impact / Hit SFX", "Digital UI SFX", "Pop / Bubble SFX", "Ding / Bell SFX", "Cartoon / Comedy SFX", "Meme SFX", "Sparkle / Magic SFX", "Riser / Build-up SFX", "Stinger SFX", "Glitch / Digital Distortion SFX", "Rewind / Tape Stop SFX", "Record Scratch SFX", "Cinematic Boom SFX", "Applause / Laugh Track SFX", "Human Vocal SFX",  "Synthesized Animal SFX", "Other", "Unknown", "None"]. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
			"soundEffectsIntensity": 0, // [Blind Test] Loudness and perceptual prominence of intentional post-production sound effects from 0 to 5. This measures designed SFX emphasis, not noise pollution and not SNR degradation. 0 = no post-production SFX, 1 = very subtle or rare SFX, 2 = occasional low-level SFX, 3 = moderate SFX presence used for emphasis or transitions, 4 = frequent/loud SFX strongly shaping the viewing rhythm, 5 = dominant SFX-heavy edit where post-production effects are a major layer of the audio design. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
			"soundEffectsCoverage": 0 //  [Blind Test] Approximate proportion of the total video timeline containing intentional post-production sound effects from 0 to 5. This measures temporal coverage, not loudness. 0 = no post-production SFX, 1 = rare SFX appearing in less than 10% of the timeline, 2 = occasional SFX across roughly 10–25% of the timeline, 3 = recurring SFX across roughly 25–50% of the timeline, 4 = frequent SFX across roughly 50–75% of the timeline, 5 = near-continuous SFX-heavy editing across more than 75% of the timeline. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
