			"speechMusicOverlap": 0, // [Blind Test] Calculate the strict percentage of the TOTAL video timeline where primary speech/vocals and background music are sounding SIMULTANEOUSLY from 0 to 5 (0 = Voice and music never ever sound at the same time (e.g., pure talking then pure music). 1 = Occasional background bed tracks under speech. 3 = Balanced (Music and voice overlap for exactly half of the total video length). 5 = Complete continuous overlap (Music stems run directly underneath the vocal stems from the very first second to the last second of the entire video)). CRITICAL EXCLUSION: If the video has NO human speech (e.g., pure music/instrumental tracks or standard MV tracks without speech overlays), this value MUST BE 0, NOT 5. MUST strictly follow this predefined range or options. Do not append any out-of-range words, explanations, or numbers.
